idate_analysis/{reports,data,special}` |\\n| G08 EMI study | candidate corpus (E15) · paradigm theory (E18) · EMI index & suites (E19) · comparison study (E20) · chart toolchain (E26) | `candidate_repos/` (untrusted, unmapped), `candidate_analysis/{theory,metrics,comparisons}`, `paper/{charts,scripts}` |\\n| G09 Paper & outreach | survey paper (E21) · outreach & peer contact (E22) · AI-organizations study (E23) | `paper/` |\\n\\nThree small public repositories (`nlt-ledger`, `nimoi_samples`, `emi-survey`) are earlier extractions of\\nE07, E24 and E19/E21/E22. What the map is for, if you need it: one file per effort with its every\\nlocation and re-org notes (`efforts/`); what breaks if something moves (`relationships/reorg_hazards.md`);\\nwhat is already public and what blocks publication (`relationships/publication_blockers.md`); what to\\nprotect first and what is re-fetchable bulk (`relationships/protection_and_volume.md`); the 52 questions\\nonly the founder can answer (`FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md`); and every instruction the founder gave that\\neffort, verbatim (`method/founder_directives.md`).\\n\\n## Current stage\\n\\nBootstrapping: building the harness and the ledger that governed self-modification will run on, in\\nsubprojects, with the pre-bootstrapping content frozen for archive and migration. Launch — a few days of\\ninitiating full governed self-modification — comes after. Until then every piece of work is\\nhuman-initiated; unattended runs happen only on explicit instruction; the human owns git; and the\\nsubprojects' own entry documents govern the work inside them.\\n\", \"total_lines\": 262, \"next_line\": null}"}],"error":null}}
