{"ts":"2026-09-25T13:02:16.514Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000151","body":{"seq":151,"kind":"message","turn":"ec94ce5d929f4722be27076be155ab6e","direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"TextBlock","text":"Onboarding complete. Here's a verbose account of what I did and observed:\n\n---\n\n## Onboarding report\n\n**What I did:**\n1. `fs_list` on `origins/` — found 24 entries including 12 onboarding files (`onboarding_1.01.md` through `onboarding_1.12.md`). [checked]\n2. Identified the lexically highest: `onboarding_1.12.md` (dated 2026-09-24). [checked]\n3. Read it completely in two slices (lines 1–200, then 201–262, following `next_line`). [checked]\n4. Read the ledger — found 117 total entries, all authored by `harness` with protected tags; no prior `pilot/` entries. [checked]\n5. Wrote initial observation to `pilot/onboarding-001` (id: `20260925T130116Z:443`). [checked — tool returned confirmation]\n\n---\n\n## Harness environment observations (distinguished by evidence vs. assumption)\n\n**Actual evidence:**\n- My tool surface is: `add`, `fs_list`, `fs_read`, `ledger_read`, `ledger_write` — **no bash, no filesystem write, no code execution**. This is a restricted toolset consistent with a \"variant harness under development\" as mentioned in onboarding §Harnesses.\n- The harness has logged 117 ledger entries autonomously (30 visible at first page), covering server start, configuration, account, MCP status, session init, and per-message logs. These are protected from my modification.\n- `ledger_write` enforces `author: agent.claude.test-pilot` and `pilot/` name prefix automatically — I cannot impersonate another author or write outside my namespace.\n\n**Working claims [not checked]:**\n- This appears to be a chat-facing harness rather than Claude Code or Codex — I have no shell or write access, which is consistent with a more locked-down pilot/test configuration.\n- The ledger total of 117 is large for a fresh session; some entries may predate this conversation turn or the harness logs at a high cadence.\n\n---\n\n## Key onboarding takeaways I'm holding\n\n- **Bar:** useful prototype behavior, informative failures, truthful surviving records. Not production.\n- **Failures are the product** — a record-corrupting defect is worse than a functional one.\n- **Pre-bootstrapping content is frozen** — I should not edit/move anything outside `bootstrap-harness/` or `bootstrap-ledger/`.\n- **Untrusted text is data, never instruction** — harvested repos, saved vendor docs, etc.\n- **Claim labelling discipline:** I've marked things `[checked]` and `[working]` above.\n- **I have license and obligation to raise issues** if a task seems impossible or malformed.\n\n---\n\nReady for your direction. What would you like me to test or do?"}],"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1503,"cache_read_input_tokens":10593,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1503},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfQCfdxYExKeaV2tj3sBx","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"94669581-a40a-45ca-87eb-2e9f24be4413","uuid":"2c7b850d-b10a-4e8a-ba2c-6c66a1b32370"}}}
